# Ignore rules scoped to the application.
#
# The project root carries its own .gitignore covering the throwaway spike tree and the preserved
# spike evidence. This file is deliberately separate so the rules still hold if the repository is
# ever rooted at this directory instead of at the project root — the repository is rooted at the
# project root and has never been pushed, and neither choice should be able to leak what the other
# one excluded.

# Dependencies. Restored with `npm install`, never committed.
node_modules/

# Build tool caches.
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment. No credential and no OAuth client identifier belongs in this repository at
# all: the coach enters his own on the application's setup page at runtime, which is what keeps
# the published source generic.
.env
.env.*

# IGNORED, AND THIS RULE REPLACES THE OPPOSITE ONE. Until 1 August 2026 this file carried a
# NOT-IGNORED note for dist/, and that note was CORRECT for the host it described: a static host
# serving a branch's contents has no build step of its own, so the built output had to be
# committed or the address would serve an empty site.
#
# THE HOST CHANGED. The site is now built by GitHub Actions from source (`npm ci`, `npm run build`)
# and the artifact CI produces is what is uploaded and served. CI NEVER READS THE COMMITTED dist/,
# so committing it published nothing and hid one thing: a fix hand-applied to the bundle would
# pass local proof and review and still never reach the coach. The root .gitignore carries the
# same rule and the same reason.
dist/
